 for j,h in enumerate(heads,1):
  p.append(f'''## {h}\n\nFor {focus}, observation OR13-R-{idx}-{j} examines {question}. Freeze the question, eligible population, period, source hierarchy, event definitions, denominator, and exclusions before viewing outcomes. Preserve original identifiers, times and zones, instruction versions, evidence available at the decision point, accountable owner, correction history, and final receipt so another reviewer can reconstruct the result.\n\nDuring {h.lower()}, the {owner} should compare ordinary, ambiguous, conflicting, unavailable-system, and high-consequence cases. Missing evidence stays missing; disagreement stays visible. Report every numerator with its denominator and show age bands and difficult cases beside averages. Geography is not a capability proxy, and public guidance cannot certify this queue, prove legal compliance, establish causation, or replace current professional advice.\n\nA reproducible result for {focus} at {h.lower()} includes the selection query, inclusion and exclusion reasons, synthetic fixtures, reviewer identity, source timestamps, duplicate rule, correction log, stop rule, and a dated retest. Any proposed change must name the evidence expected to improve, the unintended effect to watch, the authorized decision owner, and the observation that would reverse the recommendation.''')
